course: dictionary
lesson: 11244
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word worm can mean different things. Context tells you which one. In «Earthworms wriggle through the soil after rain», a worm is a small animal with a long, soft body and no legs. In «The early bird catches the worm», worm is part of a saying, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: Worm is also a verb, a word for an action. «He wormed his way through the crowd» means he moved slowly and sneakily through a tight space. Ask yourself: is the word a thing, or is it something someone is doing? That tells you whether it is a noun or a verb.
explain: Worm can also mean a tiny creature inside a body. «Dog poo can contain worm eggs, so it should always be picked up and binned.» Here worm eggs are dangerous, because they can make pets and people ill. When a sentence talks about medicine, pets, or soil, it is a clue that the meaning is about health or nature.
fact: A worm is a small animal with a long, soft, thin body and no legs.
fact: Earthworms live in soil, mix it, and help plants grow. Birds like to eat them.
fact: To worm your way means to move slowly through a tight space, or to get something by being sneaky.
fact: To worm a pet means to give it medicine that kills worms inside its body.
fact: «Lǎnchóng» is Chinese for lazybones; it literally means «lazy worm».
exercise: In «Dog poo can contain worm eggs», what are the worm eggs? | Seeds that grow into grass | Small round sweets | *Eggs from tiny worms that can make a dog or person ill | Eggs laid by birds that eat worms
exercise: Mum says she will worm the puppy this week. What does worm mean here? | *Give it medicine to kill worms inside its body | Teach it to dig holes in the garden | Wash it in warm water | Let it sleep outdoors
exercise: What does the saying «The early bird catches the worm» mean? | Worms come out only when it is dark | Birds only eat worms in the morning | Early birds are always lazy | *Getting up early helps you succeed
test: In «He wormed his way through the crowd», what does wormed mean? | Ran away as fast as he could | Dug a hole in the ground | *Pushed slowly and sneakily through a tight space | Shouted loudly at everyone
test: «Lǎnchóng» is used fondly for someone who is lazy. Which English word matches it? | Earthworm | *Lazybones | Bookworm | Wormery
exam: Which of these is true about earthworms? | They have four legs and a hard shell | *They help plants grow by mixing and loosening the soil | They can fly over the trees | They live only in the sea
